cff-version: 1.2.0
title: 'MEI-Fiber: Multimodal Epigenetic Integration with Fiber-seq'
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Meiying
    family-names: Cui
    email: meiying.cui@yale.edu
    affiliation: Yale University
repository-code: 'https://github.com/mc3365/MEI-Fiber'
abstract: >-
  MEI-Fiber is a modular Python framework for multimodal single-molecule epigenomic
  analysis of Oxford Nanopore and PacBio Fiber-seq data. It provides extraction
  orchestration, HDF5-backed storage, indexed queries, visualization, and PacBio
  FIRE co-accessibility analysis.
keywords:
  - fiber-seq
  - long-read sequencing
  - single-molecule epigenomics
  - chromatin accessibility
  - nucleosome positioning
  - dna methylation
license: MIT
version: 0.5.0
date-released: '2026-10-09'
